{"author":{"id":"40e3ba2788b3b9fc163c354afc44e5f9d225bcf0a27e679aaa878dd6135c6dcb"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1781348498,"nonce":"DIadcMRX1mMoFhxupYm8Iz+FvcU=","title":"decompressor_ultra: harden legacy Huffman path against damaged-archive bit errors","message":"The 2026-06-11 extraction fix (d747658) made decompressor_rans check the sticky bits error flag and stop treating negative bits_get returns as data. decompressor_ultra (the levels 1-9 Huffman/LZ path, decompress.c) shares the now-memory-safe bits_feed but its own decode loops still do not check for negative/short bits_get returns on a truncated or corrupt archive. Memory-safe (no overread) but a damaged archive can yield garbage or spin instead of a clean UC2_Truncated/UC2_Damaged. Mirror the rANS treatment: check bi.err at loop/block boundaries and bail. Bounded, defensive; add a fuzz/truncation test case.","files":null}]}